# Byte expansion for packed coefficient products

A checked 256-entry table expands eight coefficient bits at a time. Sixteen
lookups therefore expand the 125 relevant bits, while the proved split formula
identifies this algorithm with the one-bit recurrence. Its outer-product and
contraction semantics agree in every coefficient needed by the packed table.

This is arithmetic acceleration only. Source conventions and provenance are
in `../../../source/README.md`.
